dignity|human-worth|NOUN|Worth deserving respect|The worth of a person that calls for respectful treatment.|phẩm giá, nhân phẩm|The staff protected each visitor's privacy and dignity.|Nhân viên bảo vệ sự riêng tư và phẩm giá của từng khách.|Uncountable; respect or preserve someone's dignity.|dignity
dignity|composed-manner|NOUN|Calm and respectful bearing|A calm, serious manner that inspires respect.|phong thái đĩnh đạc, tự trọng|She answered the rude question with dignity.|Cô ấy trả lời câu hỏi khiếm nhã với phong thái đĩnh đạc.|Uncountable; with dignity describes manner.|dignity
by|passive-agent|PREPOSITION|Agent of a passive action|Used to identify who or what performs an action in a passive clause.|bởi, do|The mural was designed by local students.|Bức tranh tường do học sinh địa phương thiết kế.|By plus an agent follows a passive verb; not the instrument marker with.|by
by|deadline|PREPOSITION|No later than a time|Used to set the latest time at which something must happen.|chậm nhất vào, trước hoặc đến hạn|Please return the badge by noon.|Vui lòng trả lại thẻ chậm nhất vào buổi trưa.|By plus a time or date states a deadline and includes that time.|by
by|passing-adverb|ADVERB|Passing a place|Past a person or place without stopping there.|ngang qua|A cyclist rode by while we waited.|Một người đi xe đạp chạy ngang qua khi chúng tôi chờ.|Adverb after a movement verb; no following noun complement in this use.|by
congregate|gather|VERB|Gathering in one place|To come together in a group at one place.|tụ tập, tụ họp|Visitors congregated beneath the clock.|Du khách tụ tập dưới chiếc đồng hồ.|Intransitive; congregate at, in or near a place.|congregate
settlement|dispute-agreement|NOUN|Agreement ending a dispute|An agreement reached to resolve a disagreement.|thỏa thuận dàn xếp|The neighbours reached a settlement about the shared fence.|Những người hàng xóm đạt thỏa thuận về hàng rào chung.|Countable; reach a settlement; settlement of a dispute.|settlement
settlement|inhabited-place|NOUN|Place where people establish homes|A place where a community has established homes.|khu định cư|A small settlement developed beside the lake.|Một khu định cư nhỏ hình thành bên hồ.|Countable; a settlement, plural settlements.|settlement
settlement|bill-payment|NOUN|Payment of a debt|The act of paying money that is owed.|sự thanh toán|The supplier requested settlement before delivery.|Nhà cung cấp yêu cầu thanh toán trước khi giao hàng.|Usually uncountable; settlement of a bill or account.|settlement
charming|attractive-place|ADJECTIVE|Pleasantly attractive|Delightfully pleasant or attractive in appearance or character.|xinh xắn, quyến rũ|A charming stone cottage stood beside the path.|Một căn nhà nhỏ bằng đá xinh xắn nằm bên lối đi.|Before a noun or after be; used of places and objects.|charming
charming|pleasant-person|ADJECTIVE|Pleasant and engaging|Friendly and pleasant in a way that makes people like someone.|duyên dáng, dễ mến|The guide was charming throughout the tour.|Người hướng dẫn rất dễ mến suốt chuyến tham quan.|Before a person noun or after a linking verb.|charming
aristocrat|noble-person|NOUN|Member of a privileged hereditary class|A person belonging to a society's hereditary upper class.|người thuộc tầng lớp quý tộc|The novel follows an aristocrat who loses the family estate.|Tiểu thuyết kể về một người quý tộc mất đi điền trang của gia đình.|Countable; an aristocrat, plural aristocrats.|aristocrat
on|surface|PREPOSITION|Supported by a surface|In contact with a surface and supported by it.|trên|A white envelope lay on the shelf.|Một phong bì trắng nằm trên kệ.|On plus a surface noun; differs from above without contact.|on
on|day|PREPOSITION|At a particular day|Used to identify the day or date when something happens.|vào ngày hoặc dịp cụ thể|The exhibition opens on Thursday.|Triển lãm mở cửa vào thứ Năm.|On plus a day, date or specified occasion.|on
on|continue-adverb|ADVERB|Continuing an activity|Further in time or progress without stopping.|tiếp tục|Despite the noise, the speaker talked on.|Dù có tiếng ồn, người phát biểu vẫn tiếp tục nói.|Adverb after an activity verb; read on, walk on or talk on.|on
ladder|climbing-equipment|NOUN|Rungs for climbing|A structure with two side supports joined by rungs, used for climbing.|cái thang|They carried the ladder into the shed.|Họ mang chiếc thang vào nhà kho.|Countable; climb a ladder; plural ladders.|ladder
unit|course-section|NOUN|Section of study material|A section of a course or book that covers a particular area of study.|bài học, học phần|This unit introduces questions in the past tense.|Bài học này giới thiệu câu hỏi ở thì quá khứ.|Countable; a unit of a course; unit followed by a number.|unit
unit|measurement|NOUN|Standard of measurement|A fixed quantity used as a standard for measuring something.|đơn vị đo|The chart uses seconds as its unit of time.|Biểu đồ dùng giây làm đơn vị thời gian.|Countable; a unit of length, time or another quantity.|unit
blade|cutting-edge-part|NOUN|Sharp cutting part|The flat, sharp-edged part of a knife, tool or machine that cuts.|lưỡi dao, lưỡi cắt|The chef replaced the damaged blade.|Đầu bếp thay lưỡi dao bị hỏng.|Countable; knife blade; a blade on a cutting tool.|blade
blade|rotating-wing|NOUN|Rotating flat component|A broad flat part of a fan or turbine that moves through air or fluid.|cánh quạt, cánh tua-bin|Three blades turn inside the ventilation fan.|Ba cánh quạt quay trong chiếc quạt thông gió.|Countable; fan blade or turbine blade.|blade
artificial|human-made|ADJECTIVE|Made by people|Produced by people rather than occurring naturally.|nhân tạo|Artificial grass covers the small playground.|Cỏ nhân tạo phủ sân chơi nhỏ.|Before a noun or after a linking verb.|artificial
constitutional|lawful-under-constitution|ADJECTIVE|Allowed by a constitution|Consistent with the rules of a constitution.|hợp hiến|The fictional court ruled that the measure was constitutional.|Tòa án hư cấu phán quyết biện pháp đó là hợp hiến.|Often after be; constitutional here evaluates compliance.|constitutional
constitutional|constitution-related|ADJECTIVE|Relating to a constitution|Connected with the basic rules governing a country or organization.|thuộc hiến pháp hoặc điều lệ nền tảng|The course includes a chapter on constitutional history.|Khóa học có một chương về lịch sử hiến pháp.|Before a noun; constitutional reform or constitutional law.|constitutional
family|relatives|NOUN|Related people|A group of people connected through family relationships.|gia đình|Our family gathers here every winter.|Gia đình chúng tôi tụ họp ở đây mỗi mùa đông.|Countable; a family, plural families; collective agreement varies.|family
family|suitable-for-families|ADJECTIVE|Suitable for families|Intended or suitable for families, including adults and children.|dành cho gia đình|The cinema arranged a family screening in the afternoon.|Rạp chiếu phim tổ chức một suất chiếu dành cho gia đình vào buổi chiều.|Before a noun; family film or family event; source labels ADJECTIVE.|family
scribble|write-carelessly|VERB|Writing quickly and untidily|To write hastily with little care for neatness.|viết nguệch ngoạc, viết vội|Lan scribbled the address on a scrap of paper.|Lan viết vội địa chỉ lên một mẩu giấy.|Transitive or intransitive; scribbled, scribbling.|scribble
grin|smile-action|VERB|Smiling broadly|To smile widely, often showing the teeth.|cười toe toét|The winner grinned at the photographers.|Người thắng cuộc cười toe toét với các nhiếp ảnh gia.|Intransitive; grin at someone; grinned, grinning.|grin
grin|smile-noun|NOUN|A broad smile|A wide smile, often with the teeth visible.|nụ cười toe toét|A grin spread across his face.|Một nụ cười toe toét hiện trên khuôn mặt anh ấy.|Countable; a grin; a broad grin.|grin
currency|money-system|NOUN|Money used in a country|The money accepted for use within a country or economy.|tiền tệ, đồng tiền|The exchange desk displayed rates for five currencies.|Quầy đổi tiền hiển thị tỷ giá của năm loại tiền tệ.|Countable for a monetary system; uncountable when referring to money in general.|currency
public|shared-access|ADJECTIVE|Available to everyone|Provided for use by people generally rather than a restricted private group.|công cộng|The town reopened its public swimming pool.|Thị trấn mở lại hồ bơi công cộng của mình.|Usually before a noun; public park or public transport.|public
public|people-collectively|NOUN|People in general|The ordinary people of a community considered together.|công chúng|The gallery invited the public to view the sketches.|Phòng tranh mời công chúng đến xem các bản phác thảo.|Usually the public; collective noun without a regular plural in this sense.|public
public|openly-known|ADJECTIVE|Open to general knowledge|Made or shown openly so that people generally can know about it.|công khai|The director issued a public explanation of the mistake.|Giám đốc đưa ra lời giải thích công khai về sai sót.|Before a noun or after be; make something public.|public
compatible|work-together|ADJECTIVE|Able to work or coexist|Able to function together or exist together without difficulty or conflict.|tương thích, tương hợp|These headphones are compatible with my laptop.|Tai nghe này tương thích với máy tính xách tay của tôi.|Compatible with something; often after be.|compatible
look|direct-eyes|VERB|Directing the eyes|To direct one's eyes towards something in order to see it.|nhìn, xem|Look through the window at the hillside.|Hãy nhìn qua cửa sổ về phía sườn đồi.|Usually intransitive; look at something; looked, looking.|look
look|seem|VERB|Having an appearance|To give a particular impression from one's appearance.|trông có vẻ|The soup looks too thick.|Món súp trông có vẻ quá đặc.|Linking verb followed by an adjective; look happy or look different.|look
look|appearance-noun|NOUN|Outward appearance|The way a person or thing appears to someone.|vẻ ngoài, diện mạo|The new curtains changed the look of the room.|Rèm mới làm diện mạo căn phòng thay đổi.|Countable in this use; the look of something; a new look.|look
troops|soldiers-plural|NOUN|Soldiers as a group|Soldiers considered together as an organized military group.|binh lính, quân lính|The troops returned to camp before nightfall.|Binh lính trở về trại trước khi trời tối.|Plural noun in this reading; troops take a plural verb.|troops
